      <tei:div type="colophon" subtype="notes">
        <tei:p>This “Prayer for Peace” by Norman Corwin was first published in <tei:hi rend="italic">On a Note of Triumph</tei:hi> the most listened to radio drama of all time. The drama marked the end of World War II in Europe. It appeared, with very small changes, in <tei:hi rend="italic">The Faith of America: Readings, Songs, and Prayers for the Celebration of American Holidays</tei:hi> (Jewish Reconstructionist Foundation 1951), p.103-105 — as one of a collection of civic prayers and readings for Memorial Day in the United States. The last stanza was included in <tei:hi rend="italic">Shaarei Tefila: Gates of Prayer, The New Union Prayerbook</tei:hi> (1975). –Aharon Varady</tei:p>
        <tei:p>Recordings</tei:p>
